        "status": "GOOD",
        "word_count": 94,
        "has_title": true,
        "has_body": true,
        "description": "Improve the test coverage of scrapy.utils. Includes: - A bug fix on `_inflate()`, it could loop forever on a deflate body followed by any extra bytes. - `ffi_buf_to_string()` called itself instead of `_ffi_buf_to_string()`, now fixed. - `get_func_args_dict()` compared parameter *names* against a partial's positional *values*, so `get_func_args(partial(f, \"b\"))` returned `[]` instead of `[\"b\"]`, now fixed. - Require `pyOpenSSL >= 24.3.0`, and with it `cryptography >= 41.0.5` and `service_identity >= 24.2.0`. It allowed to simplify the code and avoid many \"no cover\" lines. - The `pypy3` tox env now measures coverage, for some PyPy-specific branches"
      },
